silm:instances_papers_01_orientation_chapters_15_witness_traceability_sections_01_what_is_a_witness_decomposition_step_3__step_per_paper_ripper_§3_witnesses_schema__witness_path__witness_ a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "The per-paper-ripper contract section 3 says: every witnesses ledger row must have three fields that constitute the traceability chain: witness_path (file on disk), witness_line_range (specific lines), and verbatim_quote (exact text copied). These three fields map directly to the three of the four witness object fields path(w), lines(w), quote(w). The fourth field key(w) is added by the cite step." .
